/* book Figure 1.2.1: The two cell plans. (A) A bacterium, enlarged: its DNA (orange) lies in the cytoplasm as a nucleoid, with no membrane around it, beside a plasmid. (B) An animal cell: the DNA is closed inside a double-membraned nucleus and the interior is divided into organelles. The small rod at bottom right is a b */
